{"kind":"assert","text":"The complete retirement-guard sweep cannot be satisfied without a tracked documentation head change. The guard implementation Workspace.RefuseCitedRetirementInCheckout calls git grep --name-only --fixed-strings \u003ctarget\u003e -- *.md against the checkout; it does not consult artifact provenance or fresh artifact statements. The exact live-dot scan currently finds seven live dot event IDs literally named by eleven tracked pages: docs/concepts/actors.md, docs/concepts/record.md, docs/getting-started.md, docs/how-to/deploy-a-resident.md, docs/reference/gs/actor-retire.md, init.md, ratify.md, role-revoke.md, state.md, verify.md, and docs/reference/mcp/ratify.md. init.md and verify.md already have fresh non-stale artifact statements, yet the guard still finds their old dot IDs in tracked frontmatter, proving artifact-only re-publication cannot clear it. Publishing more artifact statements while obeying 'no prose, source, or head change' would report success without changing the fact the next batch checks.","body":{"guard_pages":"11","known_artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8d9796c28423e4b4f436627b6132ae7b83dd8ee8","known_dot":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:1a33b0645b9bd51851cdd9d1787c63a94b993d6a","known_page":"docs/getting-started.md","live_dot_ids_cited":"7"}}